title: Keep and restore sandbox history
status: draft
created: 2026-11-24
author: Luke Carrier
approach: "Land the per-VCS configuration first, then the neutral contract, then each backend, then the orchestrator and the command line. No requirement is an assumption. Git reads its reflog through git2 0.21. jj reads its operation log with `--ignore-working-copy` and `--at-op`, and `jj config path --repo` locates the per-repo config file outside the clone. The restore path reuses the existing materialise, upload and snapshot code. A restore is one forward commit on the shared branch; no existing commit is rewritten. No new ref, record field or store is added. The per-VCS `config` string is applied to Litterbox's clone only and refused under Git `direct`."
architecture: "Four layers. `vcs` owns the neutral types `HistoryStep` and `Restored` and the `history` and `restore` methods. `vcs::git` reads the branch reflog and creates the forward commit with git2. `vcs::jj` reads the bookmark's operation history and creates the forward commit in the sandbox workspace. `orchestrator` resolves the step, checks the guards, replaces the sandbox workspace with the target tree and clears the record. `cli` prints the list and the restore result. The agent has no path to either command.\n\n{{mermaid: flow.mmd}}\n\nBoundaries. The orchestrator names no ref and no backend. `vcs::git` and `vcs::jj` never import each other. The per-VCS config is parsed in the VCS section and applied by that backend. No MCP tool is added."
technologies[4]{name,role}:
  "Rust 2024","The workspace language. No crate is added."
  "git2 0.21","Refs, reflogs, trees and the forward commit. Confined to `vcs::git` and `vcs::git_common`."
  "jj 0.47","The operation log, `--at-op`, the bookmark move, `jj restore` and the per-repo config path. Confined to `vcs::jj`."
  "arch-lint 0.11.0","The existing scopes cover the new files. No rule changes."
components[9]{name,purpose,details}:
  "vcs config","The per-VCS `config` key.","`vcs/git/config.rs` and `vcs/jj/config.rs` gain `config: Option<String>` under `deny_unknown_fields`. `compose.rs` passes it to the backend. Git writes an overlay file beside the bare clone and points `include.path` at it; jj writes the file named by `jj config path --repo`. Both replace rather than append, validate with the tool before use, and fail naming the section. Git `direct` refuses the key. FR-001."
  "vcs contract","Neutral history and restore types.","`vcs/history.rs` defines `HistoryStep { revision, time, description, synced }` and `Restored { revision, created }`. `Vcs::history(&Workspace)` and `Vcs::restore(&Workspace, &Revision)` replace the policy and mode signatures. `HistoryPolicy` and `RestoreMode` are deleted. The stub and `testing/vcs.rs` implement the new methods. FR-002 and FR-005."
  "vcs::git history","The branch reflog.","`vcs/git/history.rs` reads `refs/heads/litterbox/<name>` through `Repository::reflog`, newest first, skips deleted entries and missing objects, collapses repeats and marks commits named by the synced reflog. FR-003."
  "vcs::git restore","The forward commit.","`vcs/git/restore.rs` peels the target tree, creates a commit with the current branch tip as parent, moves the branch with `reference_matching`, then writes the sandbox ref and `synced`. It returns `Restored`. A target tree with markers is refused. FR-005 and FR-007."
  "vcs::jj history","The bookmark's operation history.","`vcs/jj/history.rs` lists operations with `jj op log -T`, resolves the bookmark at each operation with `--at-op`, skips operations where it did not exist or did not move, and returns newest first. Every read uses `--ignore-working-copy`. A scan cap is reported. FR-004."
  "vcs::jj restore","The forward commit in the workspace.","`vcs/jj/restore.rs` refuses a missing workspace and a conflicted shared commit, runs `jj new <tip> -m`, `jj restore --from <target>`, moves the bookmark and writes `synced`. It detects an already restored working copy and creates no commit. FR-005 and FR-007."
  "orchestrator","Resolution, guards, workspace and record.","`orchestrator/history.rs` resolves a step number or commit ID, forces an observation of the workspace, checks `diverged`, unsaved work, staging and an open resolution, replaces the workspace with the target tree on Git, calls `Vcs::restore`, clears the merge and resolution records and returns a `HistoryRestore` outcome. It refuses a missing jj workspace with the repair remedy. FR-002 and FR-005 to FR-008."
  "cli","The operator surface.","`src/cli.rs` gains `history <name> [--json]` and `restore <name> <step> [--discard-work] [--discard-resolution] [--json]`. It prints step number, commit ID, time and description, and the restore result. `docgen` regenerates `reference/cli.mdx`. FR-010."
  "tests and docs","Prove the design and document it.","Git and jj tests cover config application and refusal, history, restore, both guards, the race, an empty log, a missing object, a no-op, a legacy record, a paused sandbox, a missing workspace and no new ref. Two jj sandboxes prove scope. `reference/config.mdx` documents `config`; a history page explains the forward commit and the guards. NFR-004 and NFR-005."
dataFlow: "`history <name>`. The orchestrator reads the record, checks the selected tool, and calls `Vcs::history`. Git reads the branch reflog; jj scans the operation log and resolves the bookmark at each operation. The list is printed newest first with step 1 as the current shared branch commit. The command writes nothing.\n\n`restore <name> <step>`. The orchestrator reads the record and resolves the step against `Vcs::history`. It observes the sandbox workspace and refuses when the sandbox is `diverged`, the workspace has work the sandbox branch does not, a staging workspace exists, or a resolution is open, unless the matching flag is passed. It materialises the target tree, uploads it to the sandbox workspace and deletes the paths the old tree had. It calls `Vcs::restore`, which creates one forward commit on the shared branch and moves the shared branch, the sandbox branch and `synced`. It clears the merge or resolution record and returns the target, the new commit and the state. The VCS log is the only store."
deployment: "Nine commits on `history-sync/keep-and-restore`: the per-VCS config; the neutral contract; Git history; Git restore; jj history; jj restore; the orchestrator; the CLI and docs; verification. Each commit keeps the tree green with a stub where a backend is not yet implemented. Gates: `cargo test -p agentkit-litterbox`, `cargo clippy -p agentkit-litterbox --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `arch-lint check`, `bash hack/arch-lint-negative.sh`. Smoke: create a sandbox, snapshot three times, list history, restore to step 2, run a tool and see a clean plan; repeat under `remote` and `direct`; repeat with jj in a clone with two sandboxes and assert the other is untouched; set a config string and read it back; confirm `direct` refuses it."
